  "explicit_non_claims": [
    "DualPI2 availability alone does not prove a compatible L4S sender or an end-to-end L4S path.",
    "DCTCP and BBRv3 are not accepted as Prague-compliant public-Internet L4S senders by this profile.",
    "A qdisc label or requested socket controller name does not prove the runtime implementation was active.",
    "RFC 9332 is Experimental and not Standards Track.",
    "RFC 9332 delay observations are not universal guarantees; targets apply only to a frozen reproduction profile.",
    "fq_codel and CAKE are Classic queue-management comparators, not equivalent DualQ L4S implementations.",
    "A passing paired trial is not programme-level statistical qualification.",
    "No public Internet, production RAN or field result is claimed by unit tests.",
    "No host qdisc, route, socket congestion control or radio is changed by this evaluator.",
    "The evaluator does not independently authenticate endpoint counter sources or operator telemetry.",
    "Mainline DualPI2 source availability does not imply TCP Prague is available in the same kernel or on a target device.",
    "Aggregate Classic goodput can conceal a starved flow; per-flow paired measurements are required."
